Package: powersync-plugin-openmeteo
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: PowerSync integration plugin for Open-Meteo weather data
 This package contains the nymea integration plugin to fetch weather and solar
 forecast data from the Open-Meteo online service, for use by the ETM PowerSync
 home energy management system.

Package: powersync-plugin-generic-energy
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Provides: nymea-plugin-generic-energy
Replaces: nymea-plugin-generic-energy,
          nymea-plugin-genericthings,
Conflicts: nymea-plugin-generic-energy,
           nymea-plugin-genericthings,
Description: PowerSync integration plugin for generic energy things (ETM fork)
 Fork of the nymea generic energy plugin. Removing an impulse smart meter now
 destroys its timer, and the smart meter consumer, smart meter producer, energy
 meter and wallbox things integrate their current power into their energy
 counters, instead of leaving them frozen at the last value set by action.

Package: powersync-plugin-v2c
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Replaces: powersync-plugin-trydan (<< 1.15.2+etm19)
Description: PowerSync integration plugin for V2C Trydan wallboxes over HTTP
 Drives V2C Trydan EV chargers through their local HTTP API: pause and resume,
 charging current, and single / three phase mode with read-back of every
 command. The phase switching sequence itself is left to the energy manager.
 Do not drive the same charger with this plugin and the Modbus V2C plugin at
 the same time.
 .
 This package used to be the name of the Modbus V2C plugin, now
 powersync-plugin-modbus-v2c, which is no longer pulled in: install it
 separately to keep a charger set up over Modbus.

Package: powersync-plugin-edf
Architecture: any
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         libqt6serialport6,
Description: PowerSync integration plugin for EDF contracts and Linky meters
 Electricity contract (Base, off-peak / peak hours, EJP) with the regulated
 EDF tariff shipped with the package or prices entered by the user: price and
 nominal price 0-100 of the period in progress, next switch, EJP days and
 season counter, and the price slots up to the end of the next day.
 .
 Reads the Linky meter through its customer information output (TIC,
 historic mode, 1200 baud) on a serial port: tariff option, period in
 progress, EJP notice, indexes, current and apparent power (VA). The meter
 number is never published nor logged.
 .
 The plugin opens no network connection.
